cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Ontosphere"
version: "1.7.4"
abstract: >
  Ontosphere is a browser-native workbench for RDF knowledge graphs. It loads
  RDF from files, URLs and SPARQL endpoints, lets users author triples on a
  canvas, classifies the graph with an OWL 2 DL reasoner (Konclude compiled to
  WebAssembly), validates it with SHACL over the asserted and inferred graphs,
  and proposes reasoner-verified repairs. Named graphs keep asserted, inferred
  and shape triples apart through export, and every operation is available to
  AI agents through a Model Context Protocol tool surface. All computation runs
  client-side in the browser; no backend is required.
